Increment: document-centric, proactive tutor workspace.

WHY each change:
- pdf_data on Paper (deferred LargeBinary): readers want the actual paper in
  view while being tutored, not just a derived analysis. deferred=True keeps the
  blob out of list/read queries (only loaded when the /pdf route touches it).
  Migration is nullable so legacy rows pre-dating the column stay valid and
  simply 404 the preview rather than serving an empty body.
- GET /papers/<id>/pdf: session-scoped (PaperNotFoundError->404); secure_filename
  on the user-supplied name prevents Content-Disposition header injection.
- generate_opening + seeded opening message: a blank chat creates cold-start
  friction. The tutor now opens with one grounded guiding question. Seeding makes
  AI calls at conversation-create time, so failures are caught and degrade to
  tutor.DEFAULT_OPENING (static) rather than 500-ing the workspace — invariant:
  the tutor always speaks first. flush() before seeding assigns conversation.id
  for the message FK; whole create+seed commits atomically.
- analysis moved into <details> toggle: analysis is now secondary to the PDF +
  conversation; opt-in keeps the workspace focused.

